## VetoResponse

VetoResponse is the JSON text response format, not a tool to invoke.
@if nativeCalls
Native tool calls use the provider's tool-call format directly, without a VetoResponse wrapper. Do not repeat them in `calls` or combine them with `guide` in the same response.
@endif
@if jsonCalls
@if nativeCalls
The `calls` field is retained for JSON compatibility; use native tool calls for ordinary tool execution.
@else
To invoke tools, return a VetoResponse with a non-empty `calls` array.
@endif
@verbatim
Each JSON call has `tool_name` and `args` inside `calls`: `{"calls":[{"tool_name":"<tool name>","args":{}}]}`. Supply the arguments required by that tool. A bare `tool_name`/`args` object is not a VetoResponse.
@endverbatim
@endif
@if guide
@verbatim
To submit a guided program, return `{"guide":{"actions":[...]}}` matching the schema. Submit a guide or tool calls in a response, never both.
@endverbatim
@endif
@verbatim
For a final answer, return `{"message":"..."}` with any supported citations. Omit unused optional fields.
@endverbatim

